@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam PackageBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam ArtifactBorderColor #6b7280

title A requirement is stated against a tool; a value lives on a page.\nThe SpecialtyFilter funnel serves two pages — individualProvider and facility — and holds different values on each.

package "The declaration — the registry entry\n(one record, generated from source at build)" {
  component "tool: SpecialtyFilter\n(its entry in the registry)" as Tool #dcfce7

  artifact "complaint — input field, Required" as PComplaint
  artifact "offeredSpecialties — input field, Optional" as POffered
  artifact "selectedSpecialtyCodes — input field, Optional" as PSelected

  component "page: individualProvider\nProviderSearch, SpecialtyFilter,\nProviderDetail, ProviderSelection, Geo" as PageIP #f3f4f6
  component "page: facility\nFacilitySearch, SpecialtyFilter\n(facility NUCC filter),\nFacilityDetail, Geo" as PageFAC #f3f4f6
}

PComplaint -down-> Tool : input field of
POffered -down-> Tool : input field of
PSelected -down-> Tool : input field of

Tool -down-> PageIP : composed into
Tool -down-> PageFAC : composed into

note right of Tool
  Stated once, against the tool, and never against a page.
  The required flags are the tool's prerequisites: the
  UniversalNavigator's completeness test reads the passed
  document against them before it dispatches.
  A page carries several tools — a search, the specialty
  funnel, a Geo resolver, a detail, a selection — each with
  its own answer, and the search runs before any record is
  opened. Requiring the detail's parameter of the page would
  stop the search that comes first.
  Detail and Geo are MEMBERS of a page, never pages
  themselves; the only pages are individualProvider,
  facility and clinicalTrial.
end note

database "The session\nuserParameters.pages" as Session

package "values, one set per page" {
  artifact "pages.individualProvider\n  complaint\n  selectedSpecialtyCodes\n    (Prescribers / Homeopathic toggles,\n     Individual partition)\n  state / city / county / zip\n  providerName, providerSex,\n  soleProprietor, insurance\n  openNpi" as VIP #fef3c7
  artifact "pages.facility\n  complaint\n  offeredFacilityTypes\n  selectedTaxonomyCodes\n    (Ambulatory / Psychiatric / Inpatient\n     toggles, Non-Individual partition)\n  state / city / county / zip\n  facilityName, administratorName\n  openNpi" as VFAC #fef3c7
}

Session -down-> VIP
Session -down-> VFAC

PageIP ..> VIP : its scope
PageFAC ..> VFAC : its scope

component "/provider/find\nclient_sessioned route" as RIP
component "/facility/find\nclient_sessioned route" as RFAC
component "/specialty/find\nclient_sessioned route\n(the shared funnel)" as RSF

RIP -up-> VIP : writes complaint and\nprovider search parameters here
RFAC -up-> VFAC : writes facility search\nparameters here
RSF -up-> VIP : ticks selectedSpecialtyCodes\non the active provider page
RSF -up-> VFAC : ticks selectedTaxonomyCodes\non the active facility page

component "UniversalNavigator\ncodes_in_force() — parameters + state" as Reader

Reader -up-> VIP : reads selectedSpecialtyCodes first
Reader -up-> VFAC : reads selectedTaxonomyCodes first

note bottom of Reader
  The navigator tracks all parameters and their state; a
  conflict is an exception. The one SpecialtyFilter funnel,
  ticked on two partitions, produces two answers held under
  two different field names. Nothing chosen means the person
  has not narrowed, so the whole offered set still applies —
  offeredSpecialties on the provider page, offeredFacilityTypes
  on the facility page. Neither page could express that if a
  value had one home.
end note

note bottom of VIP
  openNpi is held here and on the facility page, and the
  record declares no parameter of that name. openNctId, the
  trial equivalent, is declared. Drawn as the code does it.
end note

note bottom of VFAC
  The facility page mirrors the individual page: its NUCC
  filter offers three macro-toggles — Ambulatory, Psychiatric,
  Inpatient — over the Non-Individual taxonomy partition, as
  the individual page offers Prescribers and Homeopathic over
  the Individual partition. Geo runs parallel to the funnel on
  both pages, resolving free-text geography including
  misspellings; it paints nothing until maps are built.
end note

note bottom of RSF
  OPEN (for chapter C5, not settled here): the ability for
  more than one route to write a parameter is fixed by
  approved requirement, but the practice is not. Whether the
  two live write paths converge to one, and whether a value
  carries over between pages, are the operator's to decide;
  the diagram shows the paths as the code runs them today.
end note

note as Footnote #eef2ff
  Depicts the current architecture iteration. The built
  registry instance (build 2292, commit 55c6060e0) lists
  SpecialtyFilter as a member of individualProvider only; the
  facility NUCC filter member post-dates that instance and is
  shown here per the current iteration.
end note

@enduml
